{"_id":"68a736268ec3d8323af1a5d9","nodeId":"wOogVDV4FIDLXVPwFqJ8C","roadmapSlug":"mlops","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:18.833Z","description":"# Data Lakes & Warehouses\n\nData lakes and data warehouses are both systems for storing large amounts of data, but they differ in structure and purpose. A data lake stores data in its raw, unprocessed format, allowing for flexibility in analysis and exploration. A data warehouse, on the other hand, stores data that has been structured and transformed for specific analytical purposes, often optimized for querying and reporting.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Data Lake Definition","url":"https://azure.microsoft.com/en-gb/resources/cloud-computing-dictionary/what-is-a-data-lake","_id":"6a7f4ad2cb44947debcfa5e8"},{"type":"article","title":"Data Lake VS Data Warehouse","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/data-lake-vs-data-warehouse-2e3df551b800/?utm_source=roadmap&utm_medium=Referral&utm_campaign=TDS+roadmap+integration","_id":"6a7f4ad2cb44947debcfa5e9"},{"type":"video","title":"What is a Data Lake?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LxcH6z8TFpI","_id":"6a7f4ad2cb44947debcfa5ea"},{"type":"video","title":"What is a Data Warehouse?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k4tK2ttdSDg","_id":"6a7f4ad2cb44947debcfa5eb"},{"type":"video","title":"Data Lake VS Data Warehouse VS Data Marts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w9-WoReNKHk","_id":"6a7f4ad2cb44947debcfa5ec"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:05:22.994Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d04168aa","title":"DataCamp - MLOps Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/L0Ynzo"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/mlops/content/wOogVDV4FIDLXVPwFqJ8C.md"}